# Script 1 - Pre-Cutover

Create a reusable PowerShell script that:

* Validates source and destination SQL Server versions.
* Checks disk space.
* Validates recovery models.
* Detects Enterprise Edition features that are unsupported on SQL Server 2019 Standard.
* Migrates all required server-level objects.
* Migrates SQL Server configuration (sp_configure, Max Memory, MAXDOP, Cost Threshold, etc.).
* Migrates TDE certificates and any required encryption objects.
* Captures the enabled/disabled status of every SQL Agent Job and stores it in a CSV file.
* Performs validation and generates a concise report.

---

# Script 2 - Full Backup & Restore (Day Before)

Create a reusable PowerShell script that:

* Performs parallel FULL backups of all user databases.
* Uses compression and checksum.
* Copies backup files to the destination.
* Restores all databases using **WITH NORECOVERY**.
* Supports configurable parallelism.
* Generates a concise success/failure report.

---

# Script 3 - Cutover

Create a reusable PowerShell script that:

* Disables all SQL Agent Jobs on the source.
* Takes transaction log backups for all databases.
* Verifies every backup completed successfully.
* Changes all databases to **SINGLE_USER WITH ROLLBACK IMMEDIATE**.
* Copies transaction log backup files to the destination.
* Restores transaction log backups using **WITH RECOVERY**.
* Validates that all databases are ONLINE.
* Validates login mappings.
* Validates SQL Agent Jobs.
* Enables only those SQL Agent Jobs on the destination that were originally enabled on the source using the CSV captured during Script 1.
* Ensures all SQL Agent Jobs remain disabled on the source.
* Generates a concise success/failure report.

---

# Script 4 - Dry Run

Create a reusable PowerShell script for migration rehearsal.

The script should:

* Perform FULL backups of all user databases.
* Copy backup files to the destination.
* Restore all databases using **WITH RECOVERY** (not NORECOVERY).
* Measure backup throughput.
* Measure restore throughput.
* Measure copy throughput.
* Record total backup time.
* Record total copy time.
* Record total restore time.
* Produce an estimated production cutover duration based on measured performance.
* Generate a concise dry-run report.

